        "original_id": "1f8e7a60-6ee0-5280-8509-1e9ff51771e3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Danny Bonaduce, Joseph Bonaduce, Bonnie Franklin, Mackenzie Phillips, Valerie Bertinelli, Cheyenne Haynes\n- TV Shows: One Day at a Time, I Know My Kid's a Star, The Partridge Family, The Dick Van Dyke Show\n- Networks: CBS, Lifetime Movie Network\n- Places: Broomall, Pennsylvania, Indianapolis\n- Roles: host, primary judge, child actor, TV writer, producer, comedian, professional wrestler, radio/television personality\n\nFacts:\n- One Day at a Time is an American sitcom that aired on CBS from December 16, 1975, until May 28, 1984.\n- One Day at a Time starred Bonnie Franklin as a divorced mother raising two teenage daughters, played by Mackenzie Phillips and Valerie Bertinelli, in Indianapolis.\n- Danny Bonaduce was born on August 13, 1959, and he is an American radio/television personality, comedian, professional wrestler, and former child actor.\n- Danny Bonaduce was born in Broomall, Pennsylvania, and he is the son of TV writer and producer Joseph Bonaduce, who worked on The Dick Van Dyke Show and One Day at a Time.\n- I Know My Kid's a Star featured Danny Bonaduce as its host and primary judge, and the show described him as best known for being a child actor on The Partridge Family in the 1970s.\n- Cheyenne Haynes's notable works include the Lifetime Movie Network television film Lies in Plain Sight and I Know My Kid's a Star.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
